Stop the settings form alter from breaking term reordering.

Every vocabulary form shares taxonomy_vocabulary_form as its base form id, so
hook_form_taxonomy_vocabulary_form_alter() also fires on the term overview form
at /admin/structure/taxonomy/manage/VOCABULARY/overview.

There the alter appends a handler to $form['actions']['submit']['#submit'].
That button carries no #submit handler of its own, so Drupal was falling back
to the form's own handler. Setting one on the button replaces that fallback,
and OverviewTerms::submitForm() never runs: pressing Save stores these
settings and silently discards the reordered term weights. The page reloads
without an error and the old order is still there.

Only alter the actual vocabulary add/edit form.

diff --git a/taxonomy_unique.module b/taxonomy_unique.module
--- a/taxonomy_unique.module
+++ b/taxonomy_unique.module
@@ -12,7 +12,16 @@ use Drupal\taxonomy_unique\TaxonomyUniqueConstants;
 /**
  * Implements hook_form_FORM_ID_alter().
  */
 function taxonomy_unique_form_taxonomy_vocabulary_form_alter(&$form, FormStateInterface $form_state, $form_id) {
+  // Every vocabulary form shares taxonomy_vocabulary_form as its base form id,
+  // so this hook also fires on the term overview form, where terms are
+  // reordered. That form's Save button carries no #submit handler of its own,
+  // so setting one replaces the fallback to the form's own handler: the button
+  // then saves these settings and silently discards the new term weights.
+  if ($form_id !== 'taxonomy_vocabulary_form') {
+    return;
+  }
+
   /** @var \Drupal\taxonomy\VocabularyInterface $taxonomy_vocabulary */
   $taxonomy_vocabulary = $form_state->getFormObject()->getEntity();
 
